# What the DCS image installs beside the env6 wheel (which it installs --no-deps): the wheel's declared
# dependencies, the [vizx] extra, and rasterio as a distribution. Locked per architecture (dcs-<arch>.lock) with
# the base image's packages held at the versions in dcs-base-<arch>.txt (click included).
# The rasterio is GeoBrix's own build (scripts/native, bindings), made against the payload's GDAL with
# OpenSSL 3: it satisfies the name requirement of any package that asks for a `rasterio` distribution and needs
# no PyPI rasterio (which carries its own GDAL, and on x86_64 OpenSSL 1.1). `import rasterio` is still served by
# the payload's copy. Regenerate with `gbx:dcs:build --relock`.
-r core.txt
-r extra-vizx.txt
rasterio==1.5.2+gbx1
